Let's write CSS with custom utilities using `@layer` maybe Tailwind v4 syntax. In v4, `@theme` defines tokens; custom utility classes can be defined with `@utility`. Simpler: use plain CSS classes for clay/glass effects in `@layer components`? Tailwind v4 supports `@layer components { ... }` with `@apply`? Might work. To avoid issues, write plain CSS rules (no @apply) in `index.css` after `@import "tailwindcss";`. Use `:root`, body, `.clay-card`, `.glass-panel`, `.inset-highlight`, `.soft-shadow`, `.focus-ring`, scrollbars, reduced motion. Tailwind utilities from theme colors will work.

