.glass-panel { background: rgba(247,245,239,.72); backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(140%); border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.65); box-shadow: ... }
...
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { *,*::before,*::after { animation-duration:.01ms!important; transition-duration:.01ms!important; scroll-behavior:auto!important; } }
```

Need avoid `@apply` to be safe.

### types/index.ts
Define many types. Need be comprehensive but not overwhelming.

Let's write:

```ts
export type Role = 'farmer' | 'expert' | 'admin';
export type Severity = 'info' | 'warning' | 'critical' | 'success';
export type CaseStatus = 'new' | 'ai_review' | 'expert_review' | 'resolved';
export type ReviewStatus = 'pending' | 'in_review' | 'completed' | 'needs_info';
export type Priority = 'low' | 'medium' | 'high';

export interface DemoUser { id; name; email; role; location; avatarInitials; status: 'active'|'invited'|'suspended'; joinedAt; phone? }
export interface Farm { id; farmerId; name; location; areaHa; soilType; irrigationType; plots: Plot[] }
export interface Plot { id; name; areaHa; crop; growthStage; soilMoisture: number; lastIrrigated: string; status: 'healthy'|'watch'|'attention' }
export interface Crop { id; name; category; season; durationDays; waterNeed: 'low'|'medium'|'high'; icon: string }
export interface CropCase { ... }
export interface MandiPrice { id; crop; state; district; mandi; minPrice; maxPrice; modalPrice; date; source; changePct }
export interface IrrigationRecord { id; plotId; crop; date; durationMin; waterLitres; method; moistureBefore; moistureAfter }
export interface IrrigationSchedule { id; plot; crop; nextDate; reminder; stage }
export interface StorageBatch { id; crop; quantityKg; location; tempC; humidity; minTemp; maxTemp; maxHumidity; status; createdAt; inspections: Inspection[] }
export interface Inspection { id; date; inspector; notes; condition }
export interface Scheme { id; name; category; state; summary; eligibility: string[]; documents: string[]; sourceLabel; sourceUrl; tags: string[] }
export interface SchemeApplication { id; schemeId; farmerId; progress: number; stage: string; updatedAt }
export interface NotificationItem { id; title; body; severity; createdAt; read; role: Role | 'all' }
export interface AuditLog { ... }
export interface MandiAlert { ... }
export interface ChatMessage { id; role:'user'|'assistant'; text; time }
export interface AnalysisResult { condition; confidence; alternatives: {name;confidence}[]; symptoms: string[]; explanation; nextSteps: string[]; recommendExpert: boolean; disclaimer }
export interface ApiEnvelope<T> { data:T; meta: { source:string; simulated:boolean; timestamp:string } }
```

Need `icon: string` for crop maybe lucide name; avoid dynamic icon mapping complexity? We can map string to icon component in a helper.

### data files
Let's create realistic mock data.

`farmers.ts`: DEMO_FARMERS: DemoUser[] with 6 farmers. `farms.ts` maybe include in farmers? User suggested farmers.ts; we can include farms there or separate `farms.ts`. We'll create `farms.ts` too.

`experts.ts`: 5 experts.
`crops.ts`: 8 crops with icon keys.
`cropCases.ts`: 8 cases with details, linked to farmers, images use imported sample leaf? Data files can import asset? TS with vite/client supports. To keep simple, imageUrl: '/sample-leaf.svg' from public. We'll put sample-leaf.svg in public. Good.
`mandiPrices.ts`: 15 entries across crops/states/districts.
`irrigation.ts`: records + schedules + weather.
`storage.ts`: 6 batches.
`schemes.ts`: 8 schemes. Avoid inventing exact financial benefits/deadlines. Summaries generic, eligibility described as "Check official source for current eligibility". Need "Do not invent eligibility requirements" – so use broad "Applicable to farmers meeting the scheme's current criteria — verify on official source." Required documents list generic "Identity proof (as specified by official source)", "Land records (if required)". Good.
`notifications.ts`: 8.
`analytics.ts`: chart series arrays.
`users.ts` combine demo users? Admin user management can use farmers+experts+admin. We'll create `users.ts` deriving.

`auditLogs.ts`.

### services
`delay.ts` helper maybe in `services/utils.ts`.
`authService.ts`: login, register, requestReset, resetPassword, switchRole.
`cropDoctorService.ts`: analyzeCropImage(input): Promise<AnalysisResult>; uses deterministic mapping based on crop/symptoms; returns demo result with disclaimer. Also `createCase`.
`mandiService.ts`: filterMandiPrices, calculateRevenue, getTrendSeries, createAlert.
`irrigationService.ts`: getRecommendation(input) returns { recommendation, reasoning, waterLitres, priority, bestWindow }, computeWaterSeries.
`storageService.ts`: evaluateStatus(temp, humidity, thresholds), getBatchSummary.
`schemeService.ts`: filterSchemes, getEligibilitySummary, source link.
`apiClient.ts`: future-ready stub with `request<T>()` that throws descriptive error if called; comments about Cognito/API Gateway. Need not be used.

`store.tsx` (maybe in services): AppProvider with state and actions. Need carefully design.

Let's write state shape:

```ts
interface AppState {
  cases: CropCase[];
  schemes: Scheme[];
  savedSchemeIds: string[];
  applications: SchemeApplication[];
  notifications: NotificationItem[];
  storageBatches: StorageBatch[];
  mandiAlerts: MandiAlert[];
  irrigationSchedules: IrrigationSchedule[];
  users: DemoUser[];
  auditLogs: AuditLog[];
  settings: { language: string; notificationsEnabled: boolean; demoMode: boolean; reducedData: boolean; };
}
```

Actions via context:
```
addCase(input): CropCase
reviewCase(id, payload): void
saveScheme(id), unsaveScheme(id), startApplication(schemeId), advanceApplication(id)
addNotification(...), markRead(id), markAllRead()
addStorageBatch(input), addInspection(id, note), updateBatchStatus?
addMandiAlert(input), removeMandiAlert(id)
toggleReminder(id)
updateUserStatus(id,status), addUser(user)
addAuditLog(action,target)
updateSettings(partial)
```

AuthContext separate with user, login(role/email), logout, switchRole. It can use store.addAuditLog. Need avoid circular imports: AuthProvider inside AppProvider. AuthContext imports useApp from store. Fine.

ToastContext for feedback messages. `useToast().show(message, severity)`.

Need maybe `useLocalStorage` hook for settings? Not necessary.

Let's begin writing foundational files. We'll use write tool calls in parallel where independent. But each write needs full content. Let's do batch with config/css/html/asset.

